---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — 100% Client-Side Anonymous BDSM Test"
  description="Our Privacy Policy explains how your BDSM test answers and results remain strictly client-side on your device without server tracking or databases."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <Header activePath="/privacy" />

  <main class="flex-1 py-12 md:py-20">
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-16 h-80 hero-mesh"></div>

    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <div class="mb-10">
        <span class="rounded-full border border-border bg-surface px-3 py-1 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-mute shadow-xs">
          Legal & Privacy
        </span>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-1.2px] text-ink">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs font-mono text-mute">Last updated: November 2026</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-xs space-y-8 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">1. Core Privacy Architecture: 100% Client-Side</h2>
          <p>
            At BDSM Test, privacy is not merely a policy—it is built into the fundamental software architecture of our platform. When you answer questions on this website, your responses are processed <strong>exclusively inside your local browser memory</strong>.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-xs text-ink pl-1">
            <li>No database exists to record your answers or results.</li>
            <li>No account, email, or username is required to take the test.</li>
            <li>No questionnaires or individual answers are sent over the network to any backend server.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">2. Local Storage Usage</h2>
          <p>
            Our website uses your browser's standard <code>localStorage</code> API for only two non-invasive functional purposes:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-xs text-ink pl-1">
            <li><strong>Test Progress:</strong> To prevent losing your answers if you accidentally reload the page or navigate away during a test. You can clear this data at any moment by clicking "Reset" in the questionnaire.</li>
            <li><strong>Theme Preference:</strong> To remember whether you selected the Light or Dark theme across visits.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-xs text-mute">
            This data never leaves your device and can be cleared at any time through your browser's site settings.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">3. Result Sharing & Partner Comparison</h2>
          <p>
            When you generate a shareable result link (e.g., <code>/results?data=...</code>) or use the Partner Compare engine, your scores are compressed and encoded directly into the URL fragment or query parameter.
          </p>
          <p>
            When someone opens that link, their browser decodes the scores locally. The server does not log or persist the result payload. You remain in complete control of whom you share this link with.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">4. Cookies & Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            We do not use advertising cookies, profiling pixels, or cross-site tracking scripts. Standard web server access logs may temporarily record anonymous technical telemetry (such as HTTP status codes, browser user-agent, and general request time) for operational maintenance and DDoS mitigation, but this technical data is never linked to questionnaire submissions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">5. Age Requirement (18+)</h2>
          <p>
            This website is strictly intended for individuals who are at least 18 years of age (or the legal age of majority in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly permit minors to use the service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">6. Contact Regarding Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            If you have any questions or feedback regarding our privacy practices, please contact us at <a href="/contact" class="text-link hover:underline">our contact page</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

